151
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,000
De Xwedê xwesiya te me ra bibe, Xwedê şifa bide,
 
Well may God make your mother-in-law for us, may God heal,

152
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Naha a tarî, farûcî, hûr ke, ez jî me'ne kal im, em ê parîk
nanê xwe pêk ra bixwin.
 
Now oh dark, chicken, chop it, I am also meaning old, we
will eat a piece of our bread together.

153
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Sera, sera seran.
 
Upon, upon heads.

154
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
Allah selmek, ya reb.
 
May God save you, oh Lord.

155
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Ew rihê ga me, ez,
 
That spirit of an ox we, I,

156
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Min go cem wî bê,
 
I said let him come to him,

157
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,000
E ji vir ba,
 
Uh he was from here,

158
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,000
E gelek...
 
Uh very...

159
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,000
Ew kê min mala ne.
 
He will my house.

160
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
De, em biçin kê dikare, em kê çilo kin em rûnin.
 
Come on, let's go whoever can, how will we sit down.

161
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
O, ew e xaltîk.
 
Oh, that is the aunt.

162
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
He cem te be malik,
 
Let him be with you house,

163
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:06,000
A ez em piçûkê xwiya me were,
 
Oh I am the little one of our view come,

164
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,000
De were.
 
Come on then.

165
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
Bawer bikin de werin.
 
Believe me come on.

166
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Tamam. De Efrîn de hat, xeberê bide me
 
Alright. Well Afrin gave, give us news

167
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
me... e... çawa bikin.
 
we... uh... how to do it.

168
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,000
Naha te raqemê min bibîne,
 
Now you will find my number,

169
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
me silsileya xwarina bi hev ra çêkiriye,
 
we have made the series of eating together,

170
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
em derbasî gundê Banîkê bûn,
 
we entered the village of Banik,

171
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:23,000
tiştê we me wara înî ha we û mast û ferûc û tişt ha wara
 
your things we brought here, like you and yogurt and chicken
and things here

172
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Xwedê ji we razî be, gelek spas,
 
May God be pleased with you, thank you very much,

173
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
Xwedê canê we bixwe. Te zane,
 
May God consume your soul. You know,

174
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,000
em ê herin înşallah rojek dî em ê werin,
 
we will go, hopefully another day we will come,

175
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
em ê em her û nivîndarî gundê Banîkê ne.
 
we will, we are always guests of the village of Banik.

176
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Ser sera û ser çavan.
 
Upon head and upon eyes.

177
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Xwedê ji te razî be,
 
May God be pleased with you,

178
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Silavî miletê li Efrînê, xelkê miletî me li Efrînê hene.
 
Greetings to the nation in Afrin, the people of our nation
are in Afrin.

179
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Xwedê ji te razî be Apê Hesen, te daxwazê te em... te gotin
te hene.
 
May God be pleased with you Uncle Hesen, you requested us...
you have words.

180
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Na Xwedê ji te razî be, ez kê bêjim çi,
 
No may God be pleased with you, what should I say,

181
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Xwedê ji te razî be, kê...
 
May God be pleased with you, who...

182
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Ê, bar, barê bimilê te.
 
Uh, load, load on your shoulder.

183
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Înşallah. Xwedê kerîm e. Em heta kerîm em ê
 
God willing. God is generous. As long as generous we will

184
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Kur, hemme ten,
 
Boy, all are,

185
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,000
Silavê vir re û... ji hemî milletî Kurd re...
 
Greetings to here and... to all the Kurdish nation...

186
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Aywe.
 
Yes.

187
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Silavê me ji giya re hene.
 
We have greetings for all of them.

188
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

189
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Û xaltîk.
 
And aunt.

190
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
Naxwe daxwazên te çi ne, xaltîk?
 
So what are your requests, aunt?

191
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Herin bi silametî.
 
Go safely.

192
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Me xwest em derbasî gundê we bibin, em hatin halê xaltîkê
bipirsin.
 
We wanted to pass by your village, we came to ask about the
aunt's condition.

193
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Erê welleh, Xwedê xêra we binivîse, Xwedê ji we razî be.
 
Yes by God, may God write your good deeds, may God be
pleased with you.

194
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Xaltîka te ye ha! Xwestinekê çêke ji mêj ve ha!
 
She is your aunt! Make a request from beforehand!

195
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Na welleh.
 
No, by God.

196
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Saeta we xweş be. Min bihîst xaltîk nexweş e, min xwest ez
nexweşiya wê bibînim.
 
Have a good time. I heard the aunt is sick, I wanted to see
her illness (check on her).

197
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Erê welleh, eger em di qusûrê de mabin em lêborînê dixwazin.
 
Yes by God, if we have fallen short we apologize.

198
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Xwedê rehetîyê bide te, xaltîk.
 
May God give you health, aunt.

199
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Eger ez ne nexweş bama ezê teqez rabiyama ser piyan.
 
If I weren't sick, I would definitely have stood on my feet.

200
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Înşelleh tu dê zû derkevî, xaltîk.
 
God willing you will get out (of this) soon, aunt.

201
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Xaltîk, nexweşiya te dê zû derkeve, înşelleh.
 
Aunt, your illness will pass soon, God willing.

202
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:46,000
Xwedê ji we razî be, dîtina we ji min re derman bû.
 
May God be pleased with you, seeing you was medicine for me.

203
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Tu ji kîjan gundî yî? Li Tirkiyê gundê we kîjan e?
 
Which village are you from? Which is your village in Turkey?

204
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Gundê me li Tirkiyê, qezaya Pirsûsê ye.
 
Our village in Turkey is the district of Suruç.

205
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Qezaya Pirsûsê. Çend sal in tu li vir î?
 
Suruç district. How many years have you been here?

206
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Şêst sal in.
 
It's been sixty years.

207
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Şêst sal in?
 
Sixty years?

208
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:15,000
Ez di meha heştan de bûm, bavê min çû rehmetê.
 
I was in the eighth month, my father passed away.

209
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Xwedê rehma xwe lê bike.
 
May God have mercy on him.

210
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Min qet bavê xwe nedîtiye.
 
I never saw my father.

211
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Xwedê jê razî be. Eger me qusûrek kiribe, di qusûra me
nenêrin we em zehmet kirin.
 
May God be pleased with him. If we have done wrong, don't
look at our flaw, we troubled you.

212
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Na welleh qet... Xwedê rehetîyê bide we.
 
No by God never... May God give you comfort.

213
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Naxwe em ji we destûrê dixwazin.
 
Then we ask for your permission (to leave).

214
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Oxir be, Xwedê ji we razî be.
 
Safe travels, may God be pleased with you.

215
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Xwedê we qewî bike, ehlen we sehlen we rûyê me spî kir.
 
May God make you strong, welcome, you whitened our face
(honored us).

216
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Saeta we xweş be... Înşelleh emê carek din jî werin gundê
we.
 
Have a good time... God willing we will come to your village
another time.

217
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Înşelleh, her car emê rûniştinên xweş bikin.
 
God willing, every time we will have nice gatherings.

218
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Xwedê rûyê we spî bike mîna ku we yê me spî kir.
 
May God whiten your face just as you whitened ours.

219
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:02,000
Xwedê we silamet bike xaltîk.
 
May God keep you safe, aunt.

220
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Destê we sax be.
 
May your hands be healthy.

221
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Saeta we xweş, Xwedê ji we razî be.
 
Have a good time, may God be pleased with you.

222
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Me tenê xwest em halê xaltîka xwe bipirsin, naxwe we dê ji
me ra taştê bikira.
 
We just wanted to ask about our aunt's condition, otherwise
you would have made breakfast for us.

223
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Welleh xwarina we li ser me bû, hûn zû radibin.
 
By God your food was our responsibility, you are leaving
early.

224
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Em daxwaza lêborînê dikin. Ezê nimreya te qeyd bikim.
 
We apologize. I will save your number.

225
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Ezê nimreya te qeyd bikim û emê derkevin.
 
I will save your number and we will leave.

226
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Qeyd bikim û înşelleh derkevim.
 
Let me save it and God willing I will leave.

227
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Bavê Menan em gelekî spasiya te dikin.
 
Bavê Menan, we thank you very much.

228
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:45,000
Xwedê ji te razî be, ev îstîqbaleke xweş e li gundê me.
 
May God be pleased with you, this is a nice reception in our
village.

229
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:50,000
Em pir kêfxweş bûn ku em derbasî gundê Banîkê bûn. Ez
dixwazim tu ji min re li ser gundê Banîkê hinekî biaxivî.
 
We were very happy to pass through the village of Banik. I
want you to talk to me a little about the village of Banik.

230
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Ya ehlen we sehlen. Çîroka vî gundî, gundekî qedîm e.
 
Welcome. The story of this village, it's an old village.

231
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Dîroka wî... çend sal e ev gund ava bûye?
 
Its history... how many years ago was this village
established?

232
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Nêzîkî şêst heştê kal û bavan de ava bûye.
 
It was established about sixty or eighty generations ago.

233
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Yanî esasê gund, şexsekî ava kiriye?
 
So basically, one person established the village?

234
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:15,000
Şexsekî hatî vî derî, malek çêkir, piştî wê ava bûye.
 
A person came to this place, built a house, after that it
was established.

235
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Ev ji kîjan eşîrê bûn?
 
Which tribe were they from?

236
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Wek ku tê zanîn, mala Seyidî Mehmû ne.
 
As it is known, they are the Seyidi Mehmu family.

237
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Mala Seyidî Mehmû, gund bi xwe bi navê wî hatiye naskirin.
 
The Seyidi Mehmu family, the village itself is known by his
name.

238
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Bavê Menan ez dixwazim tiştekî bizanim, navê Banîkê ji ku
hatiye?
 
Bavê Menan I want to know something, where did the name
Banik come from?

239
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Wek ku em dibihîsin dibêjin ji Tirkiyê hatiye.
 
As we hear, they say it came from Turkey.

240
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Ji Tirkiyê navê gundê we hatiye...
 
From Turkey the name of your village came...

241
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Piştî wê ew şexs hatiye gund... gund ava kiriye.
 
After that, that person came to the village... established
the village.

242
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Naha çiqas malên vî gundî hene?
 
Now how many houses does this village have?

243
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Welleh nêzîkî dused û bîst û pênc mal in.
 
By God, it's close to two hundred and twenty-five houses.

244
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:52,000
Bîst û pênc mal, çend malbat hene? Eşîret?
 
Twenty-five houses, how many families are there? Tribes?

245
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Eşîret tenê du eşîret in.
 
Tribes, there are only two tribes.

246
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Du eşîret in?
 
There are two tribes?

247
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Mala Seyidî Mehmû.
 
The Seyidi Mehmu family.

248
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Mala Ûsivê Bille, ew jî xwarzêyê mala Seyidî Mehmû ne.
 
The Useve Bille family, they are the nephews of the Seyidi
Mehmu family.

249
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Maşelleh gundekî bilind e jî, wek tê zanîn nav çiyayê Raco
ye.
 
Mashallah it's also a high village, as is known it's in the
Rajo mountains.

250
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Kesên gund da jî jiyan dikin... çawa ne? Şebeke tuneye.
 
The people living in the village... how are they? There is
no network.

251
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Tuneye.
 
There isn't.

252
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Hûn ji bîran avê vedixwin? Nexweşxane, dermanxane?
 
Do you drink water from wells? Hospital, pharmacy?

253
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Tuneye tuneye tiştek tuneye. Gundiyan bi xwe hîn...
 
There isn't, there isn't, there is nothing. The villagers
themselves still...

254
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Diçin Raco.
 
Go to Rajo.

255
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Çiqas dûr e ji vir heya Raco?
 
How far is it from here to Rajo?

256
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Sê kîlometre.
 
Three kilometers.

257
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Sê kîlometre nêzîk e naxwe.
 
Three kilometers, so it's close.

258
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Xortên we yên gund, di gund de dimînin yan bi karên din
mijûl in?
 
Your village youth, do they stay in the village or are they
busy with other work?

259
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:48,000
Vê gavê bi ziraetê û çandiniyê mijûl in.
 
Right now they are busy with agriculture and farming.

260
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Karê zeytûnan, em wek dibêjin.
 
Olive work, as we say.

261
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Karê zeytûnan, pelên zeytûnan wek karker.
 
Olive work, olive leaves as workers.

262
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Jiyana gundiyan bi giştî karekî wisa ye.
 
The life of the villagers in general is such work.

263
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Va ye naha em dibînin ku sê çar dapîrên me yên rûniştinî
hene.
 
Here now we see that there are three or four of our
grandmothers sitting.

264
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Ew karê xwe dikin, êzingan dibirin.
 
They are doing their work, cutting firewood.

265
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:15,000
Jinên gundê we hemî wisa ne?
 
Are all the women of your village like this?

266
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Erê gundiyên me wisa ne.
 
Yes, our villagers are like this.

267
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Em pir kêfxweş bûn ku em derbasî gundê we yê bilind bûn.
 
We were very happy to pass through your high village.

268
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Gundekî xweş e, wek we dît maşelleh mîna lewheyekê ciwan e.
 
It's a beautiful village, as you saw mashallah it's
beautiful like a painting.

269
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Xaltîk em dixwazin em te nas bikin navê te bi xêr?
 
Aunt, we want to get to know you, your name please?

270
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,000
Xatîn.
 
Xatîn.

271
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Xatîn?
 
Xatîn?

272
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Erê welleh.
 
Yes, by God.

273
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Kê ev nav li te kir?
 
Who gave you this name?

274
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:42,000
Bavê min.
 
My father.

275
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Tu zanî wateya navê te çi ye?
 
Do you know what the meaning of your name is?

276
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Welle ez nizanim, berê wisa digotin.
 
By God I don't know, they used to say it like that back
then.

277
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:53,000
Lê Xatîn bi kurdî tê wateya delal, delaliya nava malê.
 
But Xatîn in Kurdish means darling, the darling of the
house.

278
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:55,000
Xaltîka din navê te bi xêr?
 
Other aunt, your name please?

279
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Esma.
 
Esma.

280
00:16:56,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Xaltîk Esma em pir kêfxweş bûn ku em derbasî gundê we bûn.
 
Aunt Esma we were very happy to pass through your village.

281
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Înşelleh rojekê emê werin careke din.
 
God willing one day we will come again.

282
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Di vî gundê xweş û bilind de, we çawa jiyana xwe derbas
dikir?
 
In this beautiful and high village, how did you spend your
life?

283
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Welle gundê me xweş e.
 
By God our village is beautiful.

284
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:15,000
Em jiyan dikin, dar, mirîşk em van xwedî dikin.
 
We live, trees, chickens, we raise these.

285
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Darên zeytûnan em xwedî dikin, em diçin nav wan, ev e halê
me.
 
We take care of olive trees, we go among them, this is our
state.

286
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Jinên gundên we wekî mêran kar dikin?
 
Do the women of your villages work like the men?

287
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:28,000
Gundî jin û mêr bi hev re kar dikin. Gundê me pir xweş e.
 
The villagers, men and women work together. Our village is
very beautiful.

288
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Xaltîk halê te çawa ye?
 
Aunt, how are you?

289
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Rind e, tu bi xêr hatî.
 
Good, welcome.

290
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:42,000
Ji sibehê heya êvarê em kar dikin, bi vî rengî.
 
From morning till evening we work, just like this.

291
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Tu çawa yî, halê te çawa ye?
 
How are you, how are you doing?

292
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Elhemdulillah em baş in.
 
Praise be to God, we are fine.

293
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Xwedê wextê we xweş bike.
 
May God make your time pleasant.

294
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Rojên we çawa derbas dibin?
 
How do your days pass?

295
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Welle em rojê bi qencî derbas dikin, em bi dar û ber, gund,
tiştên wisa re mijûl in.
 
By God we spend the day well, we are busy with trees, the
village, things like that.

296
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Em derdikevin nav daran, karê me ew e.
 
We go out among the trees, that's our work.

297
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:17,000
Naha zarokên gund hûn wan fêrî vî karî dikin?
 
Now the children of the village, do you teach them this
work?

298
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Na welle ev xortên naha, karê berê ew naxwazin.
 
No by God these youth of today, they don't want the old
work.

299
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Ew karê berê fêr nabin, ew karên nû dikin.
 
They don't learn the old work, they do new jobs.

300
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Em hewl didin wan fêr bikin lê em nikarin.
 
We try to teach them but we can't.

301
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Saetên we xweş bin.
 
Have a good time.

302
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:38,000
Xwedê emrê we dirêj bike.
 
May God prolong your lives.

303
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Xwedê ji we razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

304
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Xaltîk te di jiyana xwe de çi kar kiriye?
 
Aunt, what work have you done in your life?

305
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:55,000
Karê min, ez diçûm erdê, min şixul dikir, heta cot jî dikir.
 
My work, I went to the field, I worked, even plowed.

306
00:18:55,000 --> 00:19:00,000
Erd ajot, şixul dikir, min her tişt dikir.
 
Plowed the earth, worked, I did everything.

307
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Min her tişt dikir di gund de.
 
I did everything in the village.

308
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Mêrê te wisa bû?
 
Was your husband like that?

309
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,000
Lawê min.
 
My son.

310
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:11,000
Te mêrê xwe jî fêr dikir?
 
Did you teach your husband too?

311
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Erê min ew fêr dikir.
 
Yes I used to teach him.

312
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Naha mêrê te dijî?
 
Is your husband alive now?

313
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Na welle, çûye rehmetê.
 
No by God, he has passed away.

314
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Em bi xwe di gund de man.
 
We remained in the village ourselves.

315
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Em pir kêfxweş bûn ku em bûn mêvanên gundê Banîkê.
 
We were very happy to be guests of the village of Banik.

316
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:35,000
Me xwest em gundiyan nas bikin û jiyana wan bibînin.
 
We wanted to get to know the villagers and see their lives.

317
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Em kêfxweş bûn bi nasîna we.
 
We were happy to meet you.

318
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Saetên we xweş.
 
Have a good time.

319
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Xwedê we biparêze.
 
May God protect you.

320
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Emê biçin, xwedê we biparêze.
 
We will go, may God protect you.

321
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:52,000
Xwedê li gel we be, oxira we vekirî be.
 
May God be with you, may your path be open.

322
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Xwedê ji we razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

323
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Herin bi silametî, xwedê we biparêze.
 
Go safely, may God protect you.

324
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Na, deştê nav Raco.
 
Safe travels.

325
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Na, deştê nav Raco.
 
No, the plain inside Raco.

326
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Ê deştê... Cih tenê ye yan hermeş e?
 
The plain... is it only one place or is it everywhere?

327
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Na meşa, hermeşe wa ye.
 
No, everywhere is like that.

328
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Eva kekê te çi şîv seba te çêkiriye qey te jê pirs nekiriye?
 
What has your brother prepared for dinner for you, didn't
you ask him?

329
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Welleh me got qet min nizanim te çi çêkiriye. Gotiye min riz
û miluxiye çêkiriye.
 
I swear I told him I don't know what you cooked. He said I
made rice and molokhia.

330
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Xweş e!
 
Nice!

331
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Îro em ê di cem wî bixwin paşê werin înşellah.
 
Today we will eat with him and then come back God willing.

332
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Înşellah.
 
God willing.

333
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
Te çi çêkiriye xaltî?
 
What have you prepared, auntie?

334
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Welleh me ke zê pêtik di firnê da çêkiriye.
 
I swear I've made pizza in the oven.

335
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Erê dîn! Welleh şîvê we herdikan jî xweş e! Yalla em bi hev
ra bifikirin...
 
Yeah! I swear both of your dinners are nice! Come on, let's
think together...

336
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Kî ke pincer çêkin îro ji me ra?
 
Who will make spinach for us today?

337
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Da efrîn em pincer da te çêkin.
 
Let's go to Afrin so we can make you greens.

338
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:33,000
Temam wekû ke me jî, kî ji me re pincer çêke...
 
Okay, if we... who will make greens for us...

339
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Em ê xwarinê xwe bi hev re bixwin.
 
We will eat our food together.

340
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,000
Welleh maşalleh mi berê xwe da nav gund, tijî pincer, tijî
tijî.
 
I swear, mashallah, I went into the village, it's full of
greens, completely full.

341
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Eliya tu dizanî pincer bicivînî an na?
 
Eliya, do you know how to gather greens or not?

342
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Ku ez nekim ez ê çawa bikim. Tabî'î ez civînîya dizanim!
 
If I don't, how will I do it. Of course I know how to gather
them!

343
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:47,000
Saet em dizanin, yê we miluxiye ye û pêtek e û pincer.
Xaltîkê te çêkir?
 
We know now, yours is molokhia, pastries and greens. Auntie,
did you make them?

344
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Erê, em pincer. Em jî pir ji pincer hez dikin.
 
Yes, we made greens. We also like greens a lot.

345
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Xaltîka me yek miluxiye ye û yek pêtik e, xaltîkê te xêl
tiştek... ez zanim te ke çi şîvê bikira.
 
Our auntie has molokhia and the other has pastries, auntie
you have many things... I wonder what dinner you would have
made.

346
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Welleh em jî hema dixwin!
 
I swear we just eat!

347
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Temam em gî ke... Em bi giştî hemî tiştan dixwin...
 
Okay we all... we generally eat everything...

348
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Em kî di cem we rojiya we re bibin. Ê... riza miluxiyê
yan...
 
We will join you for fasting. Riza molokhia or...

349
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:17,000
Riza w miluxiyê... Riza w miluxiyê yo...
 
Rice and molokhia... Rice and molokhia...

350
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Mane em ê nuho gihên rojiya bibin, û tab'en g... hemî jî bi
alîkariya îzna bavê me didê.
 
We will now get to the fasting, and of course... all of this
with the permission of our father.

351
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Bavê me îzna me da em ê kelem bikin am herin Raco.
 
Our father gave us permission, we will talk and go to Raco.

352
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Em ê herin bagerin, çend gundê me Raco am ê herin nan u
tiştî şîva...
 
We will go around, our villages in Raco, we will get bread
and dinner items...

353
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Erê ji bo şîvê. Rojiya me l'ser me be.
 
Yes for dinner. Our fast is on us.

354
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:35,000
Xaltiyek me li Almanyayê silavên xwe j'we re hanîn navî
gundî emîne ye.
 
An aunt of ours in Germany sent her greetings to you, the
village name is Emine.

355
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Gotiye ez dixwazim derbasî gundê Banîkê bî, xwarina çar pênc
malbetan l'ser me be.
 
She said I want you to go to Banike village, the food for
four or five families will be on us.

356
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:45,000
Naha ev silavên xaltiyê xwedê ji xêrê re binîsîne û qebûl...
bavî min... ew zîn da me, emê nuha herin Raco.
 
Now, may God write these greetings of the aunt as a good
deed and accept it... my father... gave us the permission,
we will now go to Raco.

357
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:49,000
Çi gundekî em ê herin...
 
What village will we go to...

358
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
De baş e da em meşin...
 
Okay, let's walk...

359
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Em ê naha rabin herin.
 
We will now get up and go.

360
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:58,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja ji gundê banîkê, dikan tune ye am
derbasbûn Racoyê.
 
Yes dear viewers, from Banike village, there is no shop so
we passed to Raco.

361
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:04,000
Naha em derbasî cem kekê me bîn spêda te bixêr ser kî em
derneketiye, em qestî tiştina em girtiye.
 
Now we passed by our brother, good morning to you, we
haven't gone out to anyone, we intentionally took some
things.

362
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:09,000
Malbat ji me re mane ji şeş malbatan re em ê bibin.
 
Families are left for us, we will take for six families.

363
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:14,000
Fêdî ne wî rojiye xatirê vê rojî de ev xêr qebûl kin...
 
This world is temporary, for the sake of this fasting, may
they accept this charity...

364
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:19,000
Em ji xelkê re xwarin çêkin û bibin û nexweşiyê ji derdan
derkin, em dixwazin nan em bi xwe bibin am wek baştir e.
 
We making food for people and taking it and removing
sickness from pain, we want to take the bread ourselves,
it's better.

365
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:26,000
Em naha tiştan bibin sê saetî ev... em di nav gund da me re
xaber denê... nuho am zeyt dest pê kin. Şeş şîşe zeyt di de
me.
 
We now take things for three hours... we tell them in the
village... now let's start with the oil. Give us six bottles
of oil.

366
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Bê çi zeyt e?
 
What oil?

367
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:35,000
Zeyt Nûdî... Ez tişkî min... am zeyt... xwedî nekin.
 
Nudi oil... I will... we won't keep the oil.

368
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:40,000
Şeş... Yas mîşka...
 
Six... Yas boxes...

369
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:45,000
Helawî bi çi keke?
 
How much is the halva brother?

370
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:48,000
Hevdah w nîv.
 
Seventeen and a half.

371
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:51,000
Çend? Hevdah w nîv.
 
How much? Seventeen and a half.

372
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:57,000
Dibsî bacana w çi ye?
 
What about tomato paste?

373
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Çardeh.
 
Fourteen.

374
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:08,000
Şeş yasmîşkê...
 
Six Yas boxes...

375
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:18,000
Şeş yasmîşka...
 
Six Yas boxes...

376
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:23,000
Temam.
 
Okay.

377
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:36,000
Tên tişt...
 
Bringing things...

378
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Te şeş zater yazmîş kirin? Raco zater pênci ye. Şeş jê
yazmîş ke û rûn şeş.
 
Did you write down six za'atars? Raco za'atar is fifty.
Write down six of them and six oil.

379
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:56,000
Şeş jê yazmîş ke.
 
Write down six of them.

380
00:23:56,000 --> 00:24:00,000
Şeş şe'îriye û şeş nîskik... yazmîş ke.
 
Six vermicelli and six lentil... write down.

381
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:04,000
Şeş şe'îriye û şeş nîskik.
 
Six vermicelli and six lentil.

382
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:09,000
Bê çiye ew penêr? Penêro...
 
What is that cheese? Cheese...

383
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:14,000
Pênc û nîv.
 
Five and a half.

384
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:18,000
Şeş jê yazmîş ke.
 
Write down six of them.

385
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:22,000
Cema çi ma? Em ê çi bibin? Çayo.
 
What is left together? What will we take? Tea.

386
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:26,000
Çayê... dudu vase... bîst û heft.
 
Tea... two cups... twenty seven.

387
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Dudu fase bîst û heft... Vê dikanê em dibînin gelekî sed
wereq yazmîşe.
 
Two cups twenty seven... We see this shop is mostly written
a hundred notes.

388
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:35,000
Sed wereq e her yek.
 
A hundred notes each.

389
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Şeş jê yazmîş ke keko.
 
Write down six of them brother.

390
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:53,000
Pênc em di mal derketin bes malek din heye... Keçikek gundê
nexweş e, ez hesabê vê malbetê jî dikim.
 
Five we left home but there is another house... A girl in
the village is sick, I am including the account of this
family too.

391
00:24:53,000 --> 00:25:00,000
Naha ez kê bibim gund... ji mal bang kir... tebê kes nayê
malê... em ê naha bi hev ra em ê herin cem.
 
Now who will I take to the village... called from the
house... saying no one comes to the house... we will now go
to her together.

392
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:04,000
Keke sefetê elîn bê çiye?
 
Brother what is the dish soap?

393
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:07,000
Sed e.
 
It's a hundred.

394
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:10,000
Temam şeş sefet elîn jî ji me re derxe.
 
Okay take out six dish soaps for us too.

395
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:14,000
Şeş sefete elîn yazmîş ke...
 
Write down six dish soaps...

396
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:17,000
Şeş... Are...
 
Six... Yes...

397
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:22,000
...Şekil jî te yazmîş kir... Are are... Temam e wek amade.
 
...Did you write down the sugar too... Yes yes... It's okay
as ready.

398
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:27,000
Vê jî yazmîş ke... Temam... Naha hesabê me bike... Ma faroj
jî te... Em bikin we derê naha.
 
Write this down too... Okay... Now calculate our bill... Did
you also chicken... We will do it there now.

399
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Xoce em naha... Çi gerek e we... Xêriyê...
 
Master we now... What is needed from you... For charity...

400
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:37,000
Heft hezar.
 
Seven thousand.

401
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:42,000
Heft hezar. Fatura me herû heft hezar... Me dî faroj pirs
kir... Got dore sed wereqiye.
 
Seven thousand. Our bill went to seven thousand... We asked
about the chicken... He said it's around a hundred notes.

402
00:25:42,000 --> 00:26:00,000
Em wek şeş faroj jî temam kin... Em ê naha gî ev bikin û em
barê kin.
 
We will complete six chickens too... We will now do all this
and load it.

403
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:03,000
Xaltîk, saeta we xweş!
 
Auntie, good hours to you!

404
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:05,000
Saeta we xweş rûnin... Hindikî ma pir bi hesibînin...
 
Good hours to you, sit down... Forgive our little for a
lot...

405
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:09,000
Xaltîkeke li Almanyayê û birayekî me camêr me xwest
xwarineke we û... şeş malbet li ser gund be... saeta gund
xweş, xwedê risqê gundê we bişîne û saeta we li canê we.
 
An aunt in Germany and a gentleman brother of ours wanted a
meal for you and... six families in the village... good
hours to the village, may God send the provision of your
village and good hours to your soul.

406
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:14,000
Saeta we jî xweş yabo... Xwedê ji we razî be, min jî xwedê
ji we razî kir. Saeta we xweş, rojî ye, xwedê evê ji te
qebûl ke, xwedê ji te qebûl ke...
 
Good hours to you too brother... May God be pleased with
you, may God make me pleased with you. Good hours to you, it
is a fast, may God accept this from you, may God accept from
you...

407
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:18,000
Înşellah ya rebî saeta we pir xweş e, nîvê temenê we de
bin... xwedê ji we xweş be.
 
God willing oh Lord your hours are very good, may you be in
the middle of your life... may God be pleased with you.

408
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:23,000
Saeta we xweş xaltîk... Saeta we li canê we, înşellah piştî
rojiyê em ê werin, em xwarina xwe bi hev re çêkin û bixwin.
 
Good hours to you auntie... Good hours to your soul, God
willing after the fast we will come, we will cook our food
together and eat.

409
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:26,000
Hûn ser seran ser çavan.
 
You are upon my head and upon my eyes.

410
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Saeta we xweş xaltîk, saeta we li canê we... xwedê risqê we
bişîne, xwedê canê we sax ke.
 
Good hours to you auntie, good hours to your soul... may God
send your provision, may God give health to your soul.

411
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:35,000
Baş e xweş, xwedê xêra we jî qebûl ke...
 
Okay nice, may God accept your charity too...

412
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:40,000
Xwedê jiyana we sax we de... û em jî dixwazin cam we herin
xwarinê bixwin.
 
May God keep your life healthy... and we also want to go eat
food with you.

413
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:44,000
Înşallah... Bêr cem ma bin...
 
God willing... be with us...

414
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Saeta we xweş înşellah badî rojiya am werin em xwarinê xwe
bi hev re çêkin û bixwin... Saet we xweş hindikî me pir bi
hesibînin...
 
Good hours to you, God willing after the fast we will come
and cook and eat together... Good hours to you, consider our
little as a lot...

415
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:53,000
Saeta we xweş... Mîn heyro jin û banê ma na? Mîn î çaman im
naha?
 
Good hours to you... Are we not humans and your house? Where
are my eyes now?

416
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Înşallah, saeta we xweş bi xwedê em herin û em ê badî rojiya
werin em xwarina xwe bi hev re çêkin û bixwin.
 
God willing, good hours to you by God we will go and we will
come after the fast we will cook our food together and eat.

417
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:01,000
Saeta we xweş.
 
Good hours to you.

418
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:05,000
Saeta we xweş xaltîk... saeta we li canê we... hindikî em
pir bi hesibînin.
 
Good hours to you auntie... good hours to your soul...
consider our little as a lot.

419
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:10,000
Saeta we xweş. Hûn hîro jin nîvro cem me ne... Em çawa nan
bi hev re nexwin.
 
Good hours to you. Today you are women at noon with us...
How can we not eat bread together.

420
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:15,000
Înşellah saet xweş bi xwedê em herin, û em ê badî rojiya
werin em xwarinê xwe bi hev re çêkin û bixwin... Saet we
xweş Xaltîk, xwedê qeşke ta... teştare belê... faroca ve
kirin cûck û şîrîn.
 
God willing good hours by God we will go, and we will come
after the fast we will cook and eat together... Good hours
to you Auntie, may God hold your children... washbasin
yes... chicken you did little and sweet.

421
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:20,000
Xwedê ji we jî qebûl bike.
 
May God accept from you too.

422
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:25,000
Înşallah em ê werin, û hindikî me pir bihesibîne... ev wek
xelata we ye, em dexwazin em derbas cem we bin me xwez...
 
God willing we will come, and consider our little as a
lot... this is like your gift, we want to pass by you we
wanted...

423
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:35,000
Em wek leyîstokê bi hev re... çêkin û wan tiştan xwe bi hev
re bikin û saeta we xweş.
 
We play like a game together... cook and do those things
together and good hours to you.

424
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Saeta we xweş xwişkê, naha got tiştek te kirî em hatin te
hêndikî me jî pir bi hesibîne.
 
Good hours sister, now he said whatever you bought we came
so consider our little as a lot too.

425
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:42,000
We jî xweş, xwedê risqê we bişîne. Xwedê xêra we qebûl ke ya
reb.
 
To you too, may God send your provision. May God accept your
charity oh Lord.

426
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:48,000
Saeta we li canê we, hindikî me pir bi hesibîne... Naha
xwedê xwest xêrek, înşallah badî rojiyê em werin xwarina xwe
bi hev re çêkin û bixwin.
 
Good hours to your soul, consider our little as a lot... Now
God willed a charity, God willing after the fast we will
come and cook and eat together.

427
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Înşallah ehla w sehlan xwedê çavê min re ahlan w sahlan.
 
God willing welcome, welcome upon my eyes.

428
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:55,000
Xwedê te jî selmekî, saeta we xweş.
 
May God bless you too, good hours to you.

429
00:27:55,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Ya te jî xweş.
 
Yours too.

430
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:05,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja fatura me herû heft hezar û nê sed û
